#
# How each suite verifies its subject, enforced by
# scripts/check_suite_execution.py and explained in CONTRIBUTING.md.
#
#   <class> <suite directory name>
#
# Classes
#
#   executes    Builds a program and runs it, asserting an exit value or
#               output. Detected mechanically: the suite invokes a produced
#               artifact in command position.
#
#   contract    Deliberately inspects text, JSON, or a diagnostic rather than
#               running a program, because that IS its subject: emitted IR
#               shape, a diagnostic message, a published document, a script
#               contract. Classifying a suite here asserts that no runtime
#               behavior of its feature is left unverified.
#
#   unreviewed  Not yet classified. These never run a produced program, and
#               nobody has yet confirmed whether that is correct. Five of the
#               seven defects fixed on 2026-09-04/05 hid behind suites of
#               exactly this shape -- test/loop-control asserted substrings
#               of emitted WIR while no `for` program could be built at all.
#
# The unreviewed count is a ratchet: it may fall, never rise. Reclassify a
# suite by reading it and deciding whether its feature has runtime behavior
# that nothing executes. If it does, add an execution case and mark it
# `executes`; if it does not, mark it `contract`.
#
# A new suite must be registered. New suites should not be `unreviewed`.

